# Architecture guidance

Use [the current architecture](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) and [trial protocol](../../docs/TRIAL.md).

- One Node core owns source identity, explicit versions, indexing and bounded evidence.
- Clients own model calls, planning, tools, cwd, execution and approvals.
- Source text is data. Checksums and generated confidence do not establish truth or permission.
- Prefer observed workflow needs over model-name rules or additional service layers.
- Keep preparation commands bounded, explicit and optional.
- Protocol checks establish functionality; user trials establish usefulness for their observed tasks.
